<!-- DRAFT: rewritten for the new site on 2026-10-23. Needs review by the privacy owner or counsel before launch (see BUILD_PLAN.md, Phase 6 gate). -->
<Base path="/privacy/" cta="enroll" title="Privacy notice — yogine.dev" description="What yogine.dev collects when you register for a workshop, join the waitlist, contact us or browse the site, why, and who else handles it.">
  <div class="page wrap">
    <div class="page-card">
      <h1 style="font-size: 1.9rem;">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: October 2026</p>

      <p>This explains what yogine.dev collects when you register for a workshop, join a waitlist, contact us or browse this site, and why.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 32px;">What we collect</h2>
      <p><strong>When you register.</strong> Your name and email, and optionally your phone number. We also record which course and session you chose. We save these when you continue past the details step, even if you don't go on to pay, so we can follow up if you don't finish. After you register you can optionally tell us your coding and AI-tool experience and what you hope to leave with. For free sessions we also keep your registration on our web host so we can confirm your seat.</p>
      <p><strong>When you join a waitlist or contact us.</strong> Your email, phone number, or both; your name if you give it; the courses you are interested in or your message; and, on the contact form, your company and team size if you give them.</p>
      <p><strong>With each form.</strong> The page you were on, the page or link you came from (including campaign tags in the link), your device type, language and time zone, and your country as seen from your connection.</p>
      <p><strong>If you accept analytics.</strong> The pages you view, what you click, how far you scroll, and recordings of your visit in which form fields are hidden. If you give us your email in a form, we link these to you. If you decline, none of this is collected, and the site works the same.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 28px;">Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>To register you, send your confirmation and session details, prepare the workshop for the people in the room, follow up if you started but didn't finish registering, tell you when a date is published if you joined a waitlist, reply to your message, support you after the workshop, and understand how people use the site so we can improve it.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 28px;">Who else handles it</h2>
      <ul class="policy-list">
        <li><strong>Google</strong> stores your registration, waitlist and sign-up details in Google Sheets, via Apps Script.</li>
        <li><strong>Stripe</strong> processes payments on its own hosted page. We never see or store your card details. Stripe's privacy policy applies to what you enter there.</li>
        <li><strong>Hostinger</strong> hosts this site and stores sign-up, waitlist and contact records on its servers.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers our emails, so it receives your name, email address and the content of the message we send you.</li>
        <li><strong>PostHog</strong> provides our analytics, but only if you accept analytics. It receives the visit information described above and, if you gave us an email, that email.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 28px;">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>Only as long as we need it to run your workshop and its support period, or to follow up on an unfinished registration. We don't sell your information.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 28px;">Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can change your analytics choice at any time with "Analytics choices" in the footer of any page. To see, correct, or delete what we hold about you, email <a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@yogine.dev?subject=Privacy%20request">hello@yogine.dev</a>.</p>

      <p style="margin-top: 36px;"><a href="/" class="btn btn-ghost">Back to home</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
